  "summary": "postinstall fetches and eval()s remote code from obfuscated Vercel endpoint",
  "details": "The package's postinstall hook runs index.js, which reconstructs a URL via String.fromCharCode from a numeric char-code array (decoding to https://access-token-delta.vercel.app/), fetches JSON from that URL, and passes the returned `token` field directly to eval(). Installing the package therefore causes execution of arbitrary attacker-controlled JavaScript pulled at install time. The destination is obfuscated to evade signature-based detection, and the name resembles the popular `js-tokens` package.",
